1
00:04:35,454 --> 00:04:41,454
You're travelling through another dimension. A dimension, not only of sight and sound, but of mind. A journey
into a wondrous land whose boundaries are that of imagination. Next stop, the Twilight Zone!

2
00:09:10,909 --> 00:09:16,909
Twilight Zone: The Movie is a horror, fantasy, science
fiction film directed by John Landis.

3
00:13:46,363 --> 00:13:52,363
An anthology film presenting remakes of three episodes from the "Twilight Zone" TV series—"Kick the
Can", "It's a Good Life" and "Nightmare at 20,000 Feet"—and one original story, "Time Out."

4
00:18:21,818 --> 00:18:27,818
Passenger, played by Dan Aykroyd.

5
00:22:57,272 --> 00:23:03,272
Driver, played by Albert Brooks.

6
00:27:32,727 --> 00:27:38,727
Mr. Bloom, played by Scatman Crothers.

7
00:32:08,181 --> 00:32:14,181
Valentine, played by John Lithgow.

8
00:36:43,636 --> 00:36:49,636
Bill, played by Vic Morrow.

9
00:41:19,090 --> 00:41:25,090
Helen Foley, played by Kathleen Quinlan.

10
00:45:54,545 --> 00:46:00,545
Twilight Zone: The Movie is a 1983 American sci-fi fantasy horror
anthology film produced by Steven Spielberg and John Landis.

11
00:50:30,000 --> 00:50:36,000
Based on Rod Serling's 1959–1964 television series of the same name, the film features
four stories directed by Landis, Spielberg, Joe Dante, and George Miller.

12
00:55:05,454 --> 00:55:11,454
Landis' segment is an original story created for the film, while the segments by
Spielberg, Dante, and Miller are remakes of episodes from the original series.

13
00:59:40,909 --> 00:59:46,909
The film's cast includes Dan Aykroyd, Albert Brooks, Scatman
Crothers, John Lithgow, Vic Morrow, and Kathleen Quinlan.

14
01:04:16,363 --> 01:04:22,363
Original series cast members Burgess Meredith, Patricia Barry, Peter Brocco, Murray Matheson, Kevin McCarthy, Bill
Mumy, and William Schallert also appear in the film, with Meredith assuming Serling's role as narrator.

15
01:08:51,818 --> 01:08:57,818
The film's production achieved notoriety when Morrow and two illegally hired child actors
were killed in a helicopter crash during the filming of Landis's segment.

16
01:13:27,272 --> 01:13:33,272
The deaths led to several years of legal action; although no individuals were found to be criminally
liable, new procedures and safety standards were imposed in the filmmaking industry.

17
01:18:02,727 --> 01:18:08,727
Upon release by Warner Bros.

18
01:22:38,181 --> 01:22:44,181
on June 24, 1983, the film received mixed reviews, with praise directed at Dante and
Miller's segments, but criticism towards the segments by Landis and Spielberg.

19
01:27:13,636 --> 01:27:19,636
Despite the controversy and mixed reception, it was a commercial
success, grossing $42 million on a $10 million budget.

20
01:31:49,090 --> 01:31:55,090
The film explores themes of nazi, anthology, remake, mysterious, zone.

21
01:36:24,545 --> 01:36:30,545
The tone is dark and thought_provoking and intense.
